# ergo test cannot build the generated RPC Client of limits.Limiter: a
# Client needs a Conn to a served limiter. The gateway case calls the
# contract over RPC instead.
skip law limits.Limiter.NeverOverdraws for Client: its values have no generator: rpc.Conn has an unexported field, so only package rpc builds it; use rpc.Dial or rpc.Loopback; a func NewClient() Client with no rows would build one for each case
skip law limits.Limiter.RetryAfterIsExact for Client: its values have no generator: rpc.Conn has an unexported field, so only package rpc builds it; use rpc.Dial or rpc.Loopback; a func NewClient() Client with no rows would build one for each case
skip law limits.Limiter.LimitedTakesNothing for Client: its values have no generator: rpc.Conn has an unexported field, so only package rpc builds it; use rpc.Dial or rpc.Loopback; a func NewClient() Client with no rows would build one for each case
# Nor a Loopback: it serves the limiter its caller passes in, and only a
# test picks that limiter outside cmd/limiter/main.ergo. loopback/tests.ergo
# picks a memory limiter and asserts these laws through the wire.
skip law limits.Limiter.NeverOverdraws for Loopback: its values have no generator: limitsrpc.Client has an unexported field, so only package limitsrpc builds it; use limitsrpc.NewClient; a func NewLoopback() Loopback with no rows would build one for each case
